<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federico Tinoco Granados</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Federico Tinoco Granados was a Costa Rican army officer and war minister who overthrew President Alfredo González Flores in January 1917 and ruled as a dictator. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a> refused to recognise his government, and growing unrest and an invasion by exiles forced him to resign in August 1919. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federico-tinoco-granados.jpg" alt="Federico Tinoco Granados" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Federico_Tinoco_Granados.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
